# Two images are built from the repository root: the documentation site's
# (deploy/site/Dockerfile) and the live demo's (deploy/demo/Dockerfile).
# Everything is excluded, then only what those COPY is let back in, so a
# `.venv`, a bench corpus or a stray log never enters a build context or an
# image layer.
*
!deploy/site/wheelhouse/
!apps/site/siteapp/
!dist/site/
!deploy/demo/wheelhouse/
!apps/demo/demoapp.py

# The Mojo image (deploy/mojo/Dockerfile, one file for every Mojo app it
# builds) compiles in its builder stage, so its context is source: the
# toolchain pin, the packages, the apps it is used for -- each let in by name,
# so a new one's first build fails `"/apps/<name>/server.mojo": not found`
# until it is added here -- and the three scripts that make a linked artifact
# redistributable.
# Built `.mojoc` artifacts are excluded even under those paths -- the builder
# precompiles its own, and a stale one from the host would be a silent
# mismatch with the toolchain in the image.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!packages/
!apps/hello/
!apps/blobs/
!scripts/relocate.py
!scripts/bundle_artifact.py
!scripts/binfmt.py
**/*.mojoc
**/__pycache__/
